<content>
  <section><para>Old Faithful is a geyser in Yellowstone National Park. The following table offers some rough estimates of the length of an eruption (in minutes) and the amount of water (in gallons) in that eruption.</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="5"><thead/>
  <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  Length (minutes)
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  1.5
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  2
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  3
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  4.5
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  Amount of Water
                      (gallons)
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  3,700
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  4,100
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  6,450
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  8,400
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup></table><para>Use technology to find an equation of the line of best fit. Round to the nearest hundredth.</para></section>
</content>
